## Approach

Replace brute-force O(n²) all-pairs cosine similarity with SimHash LSH (random hyperplane hashing) for candidate generation, followed by exact verification on candidate pairs only. Pre-normalize vectors so cosine similarity = dot product. Cache all computed similarities in a HashMap for reuse across phases.

The existing algorithm has three phases (union-find grouping → complete-link pruning → avg_similarity), all doing redundant cosine_similarity calls on 1024-dim vectors. LSH narrows Phase 1 from n² to ~n·B candidate pairs (B = avg bucket size). The similarity cache eliminates redundant computation in Phases 2 and 3.

Alternative considered: spatial indexing (VP-tree, ball-tree). More complex to implement, similar asymptotic improvement, but LSH is simpler and well-suited to the high dimensionality (d=1024) where tree-based approaches degrade.

